SwiftPutty local patch 0006
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   SwiftPutty-specific; could be offered upstream

Structured port forwarding status for front ends.

PuTTY reports the outcome of each port forwarding only as Event Log
text. A front end that shows per-forwarding state, and that stages
live edits so that a failed change keeps the previous forwarding
(docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 6.4), needs it in structured form.

LogPolicyVtable gains an optional portfwd_status method (NULL-checked
by lp_portfwd_status, so existing LogPolicy implementations, which use
designated initialisers, are unaffected). Each PortFwdRecord created
from CONF_portfwd remembers its configuration key and value, and
portfwdmgr_report_status() reports, next to the existing Event Log
messages: listening / listen failed (local and dynamic), request sent /
enabled / refused / duplicate (remote, SSH-1 and SSH-2), and closed (a
forwarding removed by reconfiguration). Behaviour is otherwise
unchanged.

--- a/defs.h
+++ b/defs.h
@@ -119,6 +119,28 @@
 typedef struct Ldisc_tag Ldisc;
 typedef struct LogContext LogContext;
 typedef struct LogPolicy LogPolicy;
+
+/*
+ * The outcome of setting up or removing one configured port forwarding,
+ * for front ends that show per-forwarding state (LogPolicyVtable
+ * portfwd_status). key and value are the CONF_portfwd entry the
+ * forwarding came from.
+ */
+typedef enum PortFwdStatusKind {
+    PFS_LISTENING,          /* local or dynamic: listening */
+    PFS_LISTEN_FAILED,      /* local or dynamic: could not listen */
+    PFS_REMOTE_REQUESTED,   /* remote: request sent to the server */
+    PFS_REMOTE_ENABLED,     /* remote: the server accepted it */
+    PFS_REMOTE_REFUSED,     /* remote: the server refused it */
+    PFS_DUPLICATE,          /* remote: listening address already in use */
+    PFS_CLOSED,             /* removed by a configuration change */
+} PortFwdStatusKind;
+typedef struct PortFwdStatus {
+    PortFwdStatusKind kind;
+    const char *key, *value;
+    const char *message;    /* error text, or NULL */
+} PortFwdStatus;
+
 typedef struct LogPolicyVtable LogPolicyVtable;
 
 typedef struct TermLineEditor TermLineEditor;
